# Token / context limit handoff

When you are approaching the usage or context limit (treat **~95%** as the trigger), stop starting new work. Finish the current unit cleanly and leave a handoff brief.

## Before you stop

1. **Stop expanding scope.** Do not begin a new milestone, file, or large refactor.
2. **Land in a neat place:**
   - Complete or cleanly revert half-finished edits (no broken syntax, no half-applied renames).
   - Leave the tree buildable/testable for whatever was in progress, or clearly mark unfinished files.
   - Prefer committing only if Operator already asked for a commit; otherwise leave a clean working tree description in the brief.
3. **Do not improvise past the master spec.** If blocked, say so in the brief.

## Handoff brief (required)

Write or update a Markdown brief at:

`docs/handoffs/HANDOFF_YYYY-MM-DD_HHMM.md`

(Use America/Denver local time in the filename when known.)

The brief must include:

| Section | Contents |
|---|---|
| **Status** | One-line: what milestone/task was in progress and why you stopped (token/context limit). |
| **Done** | Bullet list of what was completed and verified (tests run, files created). |
| **In progress** | Exact file paths and what is unfinished; include line/region hints if useful. |
| **Not started** | Remaining work for the current milestone only. |
| **Repo state** | Branch, uncommitted files, last commit hash if any, whether anything was pushed. |
| **Commands to run next** | Copy-pasteable next steps for Claude Code (e.g. `python3 -m unittest …`). |
| **Open questions / blockers** | VERIFY items, missing Operator input, failed assumptions. |
| **Spec pointers** | Section numbers in `TRADING_BOT_MASTER_SPEC.md` that govern the next work. |

End the brief with:

```text
PICKUP: Start from "Not started" / "In progress". Do not redo "Done".
```

## After writing the brief

Tell Operator the brief path in one short message. Do not continue building past the neat stopping point.

**Claude Code pickup:** `CLAUDE.md` requires reading the newest file in `docs/handoffs/` before any other work after a stop.
